  "question": {
    "text": "Let <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>4</mn><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>6</mn></math>&nbsp;and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></math>&nbsp;be three tangent lines to the circle <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>h</mi><msup><mo>)</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mo>(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>k</mi><msup><mo>)</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math>. Then <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>h</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>k</mi></math> is equal to :",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "R98zY",
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>5</mn></math>",
